I'm staying with my answer: `COUNT(*)` counts rows with NULLs. We disagree, and more repetition on either side won't resolve it. The test will.

```sql
CREATE TABLE t (x INT, y INT);
INSERT INTO t VALUES (1, 1), (NULL, 2), (NULL, NULL);

SELECT COUNT(*), COUNT(x), COUNT(y) FROM t;
